From: avlo-py-build <py-build@avlo.local>
Subject: [PATCH] AVLO: owned-restore seam — delete upstream container, add _avloRestore

P2 owned snapshots: the host (web/src/core/py + the py-build harness)
owns the container format (AVS2), capture I/O, and the restore order
end-to-end. The fork keeps only thin hooks.
- pyodide.ts: DELETE prepareSnapshot and config _loadSnapshot/
  _makeSnapshot/_snapshotDeserializer. ADD _avloRestore.preBlit — when
  present, boot with noInitialRun (runtime init + preRun + main-module
  ctors still run; main()/CPython init is skipped) and run
  preBlit(Module, API) in bootstrapPyodide BEFORE finalizeBootstrap:
  the host validates, pre-grows via Module.growMemory (0001 export —
  upstream's INITIAL_MEMORY resize was a no-op against this glue since
  memory is wasm-exported), replays DSOs at recorded bases (0005 +
  emsdk dsoBaseHook), blits the heap, and returns the SnapshotConfig
  finalizeBootstrap resumes from (upstream syncUpSnapshotLoad1/2).
- snapshot.ts: DELETE makeSnapshot/restoreSnapshot + the binary
  container helpers. KEEP serializeHiwireState, getExpectedKeys,
  syncUpSnapshotLoad1/2, makeGlobalsProxy.
- api.ts: DELETE the makeMemorySnapshot static and the _makeSnapshot
  jsglobals proxy wrap (capture is host-driven via
  API.serializeHiwireState; with the js-module registration gone (0008)
  no hiwire entry needs the access-path proxy).
- types.ts/emscripten-settings.ts accordingly (INITIAL_MEMORY seam
  dead).

